\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Trajectory visualizations for the three canonical test problems. (a)\nobreakspace  {}The Kepler elliptical orbit ($e = 0.5$) closes to within $0.051\%$ of the initial position after one period, validating the integrator's accuracy for periodic orbits. (b)\nobreakspace  {}The Chenciner--Montgomery figure-eight choreography \citep  {chenciner2000} maintains its periodic pattern with energy conservation at machine precision ($|\Delta E/E_0| \sim 10^{-15}$). (c)\nobreakspace  {}A Plummer sphere \citep  {plummer1911} with $N = 500$ particles showing the initial virialized configuration.\relax }}{11}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:canonical}{{6}{11}{Trajectory visualizations for the three canonical test problems. (a)~The Kepler elliptical orbit ($e = 0.5$) closes to within $0.051\%$ of the initial position after one period, validating the integrator's accuracy for periodic orbits. (b)~The Chenciner--Montgomery figure-eight choreography \citep {chenciner2000} maintains its periodic pattern with energy conservation at machine precision ($|\Delta E/E_0| \sim 10^{-15}$). (c)~A Plummer sphere \citep {plummer1911} with $N = 500$ particles showing the initial virialized configuration.\relax }{figure.caption.24}{}}
